Source: plzig
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: PL/Zig maintainers <plzig@invalid>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 postgresql-server-dev-all (>= 217~),
 cmake,
 patch,
 plzig-zig-toolchain (>= 0.17.1),
 plzig-zig-toolchain (<< 0.17.2~),
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-plzig
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${postgresql:Depends},
 plzig-zig-toolchain (>= 0.17.1),
 plzig-zig-toolchain (<< 0.17.2~),
Description: PL/Zig procedural language for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
 PL/Zig lets PostgreSQL functions, procedures, triggers and DO blocks be
 written in Zig 0.17.1. Function bodies are compiled by the Zig compiler
 (package plzig-zig-toolchain, the default plzig.zig_path) to WebAssembly
 and run in an embedded interpreter (WAMR) inside the backend.
 .
 The compiler runs in a sandbox. Its default mode,
 plzig.compiler_sandbox = require, needs Landlock ABI 6 or later (Linux
 6.12 or newer) and seccomp. On older kernels (the stock kernels of
 Debian 12 and Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04, for example) CREATE FUNCTION ...
 LANGUAGE plzig refuses to compile until an administrator lowers
 plzig.compiler_sandbox in postgresql.conf, which runs the compiler with
 fewer restrictions (see the README's security model).
 .
 USAGE on the language is not granted to PUBLIC.
